  "feature_name": "output-clarity-ladder",
  "description": "## Original Description\nAdd a canonical \"output-clarity-ladder\" skill to sdd-mcp-server, based on the user's Output Clarity Ladder document. The skill makes explanation, summary, and teaching replies easier for people to check. It writes about 80% of the way to ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English by default, and moves up a ladder (diagram, self-contained HTML page, explainer video) only when the next format makes the same facts easier to understand. Requested artifacts (email, resume, code), one-line statuses, and yes/no answers keep their requested form. The skill must render for Claude Code, Codex, and OMP. Unlike the manual-only SDD workflow skills, it must be model-invocable so it applies automatically, and root guidance must point to it.\n\n## Core Features (What)\n1) Canonical skills/output-clarity-ladder skill with the four-step ladder and the 80% ASD-STE100 writing rules; 2) rendered for Claude Code, Codex, and OMP; 3) model-invocable as an explicit exception to manual-only workflow skill rendering; 4) root guidance for each target points to it; 5) tests cover rendering, invocation policy, and skill size. Video or narration generation tooling and API key storage; an automated ASD-STE100 approved-word checker or dictionary.",
